%description:

Tcp.windowUpdateAfterRead:on -- the read sends the open window at once.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "true: as Linux (__tcp_cleanup_rbuf()), a READ after which the receiver can
offer at least twice the window that is still open sends that window at once in an ACK; false:
the new window goes with the next ACK".

The classes: off (false, the default) and on (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code: at a
READ of the application, TcpConnection::process_READ() sends an ACK when the receiver can
offer at least twice the window that is still open, with true; with false, the new window goes
with the next ACK. Only an explicit READ, without auto-read, is such a read. This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host2, whose application does not read (no auto-read); host1 sends 100000
bytes, and the window of host2 falls below one segment; host1 sends no segment into it. At 0.6
s, the application of host2 reads 65535 bytes. Observation: level 1, host2 sends an ACK with an open window in the instant of the read.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowUpdateAfterRead
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.windowUpdateAfterRead
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpWindowUpdateAfterReadOn")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.synBit == false && tcp.window < 1448")
             .describe("the ACK of host2 that leaves less than one segment open")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.6).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.accepted(0).read(65535); })
                 .describe("the application of host2 reads 65535 bytes"))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.synBit == false && tcp.window > 0")
             .describe("the window update of host2")
             .within(0.001));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowUpdateAfterReadOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.windowUpdateAfterRead = true    # the parameter under test
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpWindowUpdateAfterReadOn: PASS
